---
/**
 * Interactive payoff explorer for long-term transmission rights.
 * Fixed scenario: 1 MW right on border A → B, bought at €10/MWh.
 * A slider sets the realised day-ahead price spread; two panels show
 * what a PTR (with use-it-or-sell-it) and an FTR option pay out.
 */
---

<figure class="not-prose border-border my-6 rounded-lg border p-4 sm:p-5" data-rp>
  <p class="text-sm font-medium">
    You bought a transmission right: 1 MW on the border A → B, auction price
    €10/MWh.
  </p>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1 text-sm">
    Months later, delivery day arrives. Drag to set what the day-ahead price
    spread (B − A) actually turned out to be:
  </p>

  <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-4">
    <input
      type="range"
      min="-20"
      max="50"
      step="1"
      value="25"
      data-rp-slider
      class="accent-primary w-full"
      aria-label="Realised day-ahead price spread in euro per megawatt hour"
    />
    <span
      class="border-border w-28 shrink-0 rounded-md border px-2 py-1 text-center font-mono text-sm"
      data-rp-spread></span>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="border-border rounded-md border p-3">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase">
        Physical right (PTR)
        <span class="text-muted-foreground ml-1 font-normal">with use-it-or-sell-it</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 min-h-[4.5rem] text-sm leading-relaxed" data-rp-ptr-text></p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Payout <span class="font-mono" data-rp-ptr-pay></span> − price paid
        €10 = <span class="font-mono font-semibold" data-rp-ptr-net></span>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="border-border rounded-md border p-3">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase">
        Financial right (FTR)
        <span class="text-muted-foreground ml-1 font-normal">option</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 min-h-[4.5rem] text-sm leading-relaxed" data-rp-ftr-text></p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Payout <span class="font-mono" data-rp-ftr-pay></span> − price paid
        €10 = <span class="font-mono font-semibold" data-rp-ftr-net></span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="text-muted-foreground mt-3 border-t pt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">
    Move the slider across the whole range: the two payouts never differ.
    That is the point — once the day-ahead market is coupled, a physical
    right with use-it-or-sell-it is financially identical to a financial
    right. The only thing the PTR adds is the option to schedule the flow
    yourself, which coupling already does optimally. Hence Europe's ongoing
    conversion from PTRs to FTRs.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-rp]').forEach((root) => {
    const slider = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rp-slider]')!;
    const q = (sel: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(sel)!;
    const PRICE_PAID = 10;
    const eur = (v: number) =>
      `${v < 0 ? '−' : ''}€${Math.abs(v).toFixed(0)}`;

    function render() {
      const spread = Number(slider.value);
      const payout = Math.max(spread, 0);
      const net = payout - PRICE_PAID;

      q('[data-rp-spread]').textContent = `${eur(spread)}/MWh`;

      q('[data-rp-ptr-text]').textContent =
        spread > 0
          ? `B is €${spread} more expensive: you can nominate the physical flow and earn the spread — or do nothing, in which case use-it-or-sell-it hands the capacity to the day-ahead auction and pays you the same €${spread}.`
          : 'The spread is zero or negative: flowing A → B would lose money, so you nominate nothing. Use-it-or-sell-it resells the capacity, worth €0 in this direction.';

      q('[data-rp-ftr-text]').textContent =
        spread > 0
          ? `Purely financial: no nomination, no scheduling. The right simply pays you the positive day-ahead spread, €${spread}.`
          : 'Purely financial: the spread is not positive, so the option pays €0. You never owe money on the downside.';

      for (const kind of ['ptr', 'ftr']) {
        q(`[data-rp-${kind}-pay]`).textContent = eur(payout);
        const netEl = q(`[data-rp-${kind}-net]`);
        netEl.textContent = `${eur(net)}/MWh`;
        netEl.style.color = net >= 0 ? 'var(--chart-2)' : 'var(--chart-5)';
      }
    }

    slider.addEventListener('input', render);
    render();
  });
</script>
